INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(97,'test_debug','{"call_id": "call_YljrcjciE8HfQolEVNytTxX4", "output": "The Ontario Drug Benefit (ODB) formulary includes several diabetes medications, but not all are covered. Here''s a summary of covered and non-covered diabetes medications:\n\n### Covered Medications\n1. **Tresiba (Insulin Degludec)**\n   - **DIN**: 02467887\n   - **Strength**: 200U/mL, Inj Sol-Flextouch Pref Pen 3x3mL Pack\n   - **Classification**: Anti-diabetic Agent (Long-acting Insulin)\n   - **Coverage**: General Benefit\n   - **Link**: [Tresiba DIN 02467887](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02467887)\n\n2. **Tresiba (Insulin Degludec)**\n   - **DIN**: 02467860\n   - **Strength**: 100U/mL, Inj Sol-3X5mL Cart Pack\n   - **Classification**: Anti-diabetic Agent (Long-acting Insulin)\n   - **Coverage**: General Benefit\n   - **Link**: [Tresiba DIN 02467860](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02467860)\n\n3. **Tresiba (Insulin Degludec)**\n   - **DIN**: 02467879\n   - **Strength**: 100U/mL, Inj Sol-Flextouch Pref Pen 5x3mL Pack\n   - **Classification**: Anti-diabetic Agent (Long-acting Insulin)\n   - **Coverage**: General Benefit\n   - **Link**: [Tresiba DIN 02467879](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02467879)\n\n### Non-Covered Medications\n- **Diabeta (Glyburide)**\n  - **DIN**: 02224569 and 02224550\n  - **Strengths**: 5mg and 2.5mg Tablets\n  - **Coverage**: Not a benefit under ODB\n  - **Links**: [Glyburide DIN 02224569](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02224569) | [Glyburide DIN 02224550](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02224550)\n\n### Summary\nWhile Tresiba is covered under the ODB as a long-acting insulin, medications like Glyburide (Diabeta) are not covered. Always verify with current ODB listings as medications and coverage can change.", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-28 23:29:26');
